   "text": "BEGIN;\n  SELECT date, total_inventory, total_reserved\n    FROM room_type_inventory\n   WHERE hotel_id=245 AND room_type_id=1001\n     AND date >= '2026-06-01' AND date < '2026-06-04'\n   FOR UPDATE;               -- transaction 2 now BLOCKS here\n  for each night:\n      if total_reserved + 1 > total_inventory * 1.10: ROLLBACK; 409\n  UPDATE ... SET total_reserved = total_reserved + 1 ...;\nCOMMIT;                      -- lock released, txn 2 proceeds",
   "originalText": "BEGIN;\n  SELECT date, total_inventory, total_reserved\n    FROM room_type_inventory\n   WHERE hotel_id=245 AND room_type_id=1001\n     AND date >= '2026-06-01' AND date < '2026-06-04'\n   FOR UPDATE;               -- transaction 2 now BLOCKS here\n  for each night:\n      if total_reserved + 1 > total_inventory * 1.10: ROLLBACK; 409\n  UPDATE ... SET total_reserved = total_reserved + 1 ...;\nCOMMIT;                      -- lock released, txn 2 proceeds",
   "fontSize": 11,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "o1c",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "o1n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 872,
   "width": 777,
   "height": 120,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100026,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700182,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Correct by construction, and the BEST option under heavy contention: a lock queue makes steady progress\nwhile optimistic approaches burn CPU on rollbacks. The costs are real, though. Locks are held for the\nWHOLE transaction, so the transaction must contain nothing slow - which is exactly why payment sits\noutside it. Multi-night bookings lock several rows, so two bookings with overlapping, differently-\nordered date ranges can DEADLOCK - mitigated by always locking in date order, which the range scan gives\nnaturally, but the application must still handle a deadlock rollback and retry. And a FOR UPDATE over a\n14-night stay locks 14 rows, blocking any overlapping booking even for a single night that is not\ncontended.",
   "originalText": "Correct by construction, and the BEST option under heavy contention: a lock queue makes steady progress\nwhile optimistic approaches burn CPU on rollbacks. The costs are real, though. Locks are held for the\nWHOLE transaction, so the transaction must contain nothing slow - which is exactly why payment sits\noutside it. Multi-night bookings lock several rows, so two bookings with overlapping, differently-\nordered date ranges can DEADLOCK - mitigated by always locking in date order, which the range scan gives\nnaturally, but the application must still handle a deadlock rollback and retry. And a FOR UPDATE over a\n14-night stay locks 14 rows, blocking any overlapping booking even for a single night that is not\ncontended.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "o2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 662,
   "width": 446,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100027,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700189,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "2   optimistic - take no lock, detect at write time",
   "originalText": "2   optimistic - take no lock, detect at write time",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "o2c",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 690,
   "width": 800,
   "height": 170,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
