  },
  {
   "id": "dl",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1730,
   "width": 604,
   "height": 21,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100093,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700651,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Choosing - and keeping a mechanism that should never fire",
   "originalText": "Choosing - and keeping a mechanism that should never fire",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "pick1",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1768,
   "width": 820,
   "height": 44,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "#a7f3d0",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100094,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700658,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "pick1_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "pick1_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 1781,
   "width": 804,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100095,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700665,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "PRIMARY   the atomic conditional UPDATE",
   "originalText": "PRIMARY   the atomic conditional UPDATE",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "pick1",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "pick1n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1826,
   "width": 502,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100096,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700672,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "No read-then-write gap, no retry loop, no version column, and it\nencodes the overbooking rule in the same expression that provides\nthe atomicity. It performs well under both low and high contention,\nand the affected-row count gives multi-night correctness for free.",
   "originalText": "No read-then-write gap, no retry loop, no version column, and it\nencodes the overbooking rule in the same expression that provides\nthe atomicity. It performs well under both low and high contention,\nand the affected-row count gives multi-night correctness for free.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "pick2",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 900,
   "y": 1768,
   "width": 780,
   "height": 44,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "#fef3c7",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100097,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700679,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "pick2_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "pick2_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 908,
   "y": 1781,
   "width": 764,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#374151",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100098,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700686,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "BACKSTOP   the CHECK constraint",
   "originalText": "BACKSTOP   the CHECK constraint",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "center",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "pick2",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "pick2n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 900,
   "y": 1826,
   "width": 554,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100099,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700693,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Kept even though option 4 makes it unreachable, because it is the only\nmechanism no code path can bypass. Its job changes from 'enforce the rule'\nto 'MAKE A BUG IN THE ENFORCEMENT LOUD' - the same defence-in-depth\nreasoning as the URL shortener's retained unique index. And because it\nshould never trigger, an alert on any violation is meaningful.\nPlus UNIQUE(reservation_id) for Race A, which is orthogonal.",
   "originalText": "Kept even though option 4 makes it unreachable, because it is the only\nmechanism no code path can bypass. Its job changes from 'enforce the rule'\nto 'MAKE A BUG IN THE ENFORCEMENT LOUD' - the same defence-in-depth\nreasoning as the URL shortener's retained unique index. And because it\nshould never trigger, an alert on any violation is meaningful.\nPlus UNIQUE(reservation_id) for Race A, which is orthogonal.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1938,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100100,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700700,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Why not pessimistic, given that contention is the real load profile and pessimistic is best under contention? Because option\n4's lock is held for the duration of ONE STATEMENT - microseconds - so there is no meaningful contention window left to queue\non. Pessimistic locking wins when the TRANSACTION is long, and the whole point of moving payment outside the transaction was\nto make it short. Having done that, the lock-free option is strictly better.",
   "originalText": "Why not pessimistic, given that contention is the real load profile and pessimistic is best under contention? Because option\n4's lock is held for the duration of ONE STATEMENT - microseconds - so there is no meaningful contention window left to queue\non. Pessimistic locking wins when the TRANSACTION is long, and the whole point of moving payment outside the transaction was\nto make it short. Having done that, the lock-free option is strictly better.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2030,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100101,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700707,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "When pessimistic WOULD be right: if the booking decision genuinely required application logic that cannot be expressed in SQL\n- a fraud check, a loyalty-tier calculation, a multi-room-type group booking with cross-type rules. Then you need the read and\nthe write in the same guarded window, and FOR UPDATE is the tool. Group bookings are named elsewhere as unbuilt, so this is\nnot hypothetical.",
   "originalText": "When pessimistic WOULD be right: if the booking decision genuinely required application logic that cannot be expressed in SQL\n- a fraud check, a loyalty-tier calculation, a multi-room-type group booking with cross-type rules. Then you need the read and\nthe write in the same guarded window, and FOR UPDATE is the tool. Group bookings are named elsewhere as unbuilt, so this is\nnot hypothetical.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2122,
   "width": 995,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
